      "type": "beneficial",
      "mechanism": "pest_repellent",
      "description": "Thyme's volatile oils (thymol, carvacrol) deter cabbage moth (Pieris rapae). Most effective when planted as a perimeter border around brassica beds.",
      "strength": "moderate",
      "source": "Cornell Cooperative Extension; Cunningham, Great Garden Companions"
    },
    {
